1012 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (n the actual combat footage that surfaces in Russian Telegram channels, there is many times a stunning lack of evidence. They sometimes include soldiers firing weapons and supposedly getting hits. Historically, there is great precedent for overclaiming kills. Sometimes a field of destroyed Russian vehicles can be turned into a reversal of a Ukrainian offensive with some creative changes to the video title. An interesting claim to look at here is the Russians using their tanks as indirect artillery fire. The claim here is that these tanks can hit targets up to 10km away. The most modern Russian tank in Ukraine right now, the T-90 series, has a maximum effective range of 6km, to say nothing of the museum pieces that have also been deployed, such as unmodernised T-62s. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
